     "user": "List 3DCP mortars from the literature whose static yield stress after 60 minutes of rest exceeds 10 kPa.",
     "text": "I’ll check the database schema first, then query 3DCP mortar records and their reported rest-conditioned static yield stress values.\nThe schema includes both measured rest time on observations and paper-level 3DCP labels. I’ll use those fields to filter measured mortar values at a 60-minute rest, then return the source identifiers and mix names for qualifying records.\nI found **7 literature 3DCP mortar mixes** with a measured static yield stress above 10 kPa after 60 minutes of rest:\n\n| Paper (DOI) | Mix | Static yield stress |\n|---|---|---:|\n| [2025 paper](https://doi.org/10.1080/21650373.2025.2529994), *Rheological, mechanical and fire resistance performance of waste glass activated geopolymers for concrete 3D printing* | 50S/50F | 40 kPa |\n| Same paper | 50S/35F/15G | 34 kPa |\n| Same paper | 50S/20F/30G | 21 kPa |\n| Same paper | 50S/0F/50G | 15 kPa |\n| [2022 paper](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.conbuildmat.2022.127618), *Matric suction of fine aggregates and its contribution to the shape stability of 3D printed cementitious materials* | 30% silica sand replacement | 19.86 kPa |\n| Same paper | 20% silica sand replacement | 18.91 kPa |\n| Same paper | 10% silica sand replacement | 13.04 kPa |\n\nThe 2025 paper values are reported in Section 4.3.2; the 2022 paper values are from Table 2. All seven records are text/table values rather than figure-only extractions.\n",
